# Changes

## 0.2.3 - 2026-09-03

* Refined `atcf-sanity` operator output after the first live AL052026 replay
  test without broadening its failure rules.
* Shows source, adapter, and ASGS advisory identities separately, preserving
  the adapter's raw token (for example `03`) alongside normalized identity.
* Adds an explicit hotstart-to-advisory timeline delta so a legitimate
  nowcast advance (for example +12h) is visible separately from a collapsed
  generated scenario clock.
* Deduplicates identical scenario clock observations in human output while
  retaining every property-file observation in structured JSON.
* Aggregates repeated scenario failures into one assessment per underlying
  condition, with affected scenarios listed, while retaining raw scenario
  issue evidence in JSON.

## 0.2.2 - 2026-09-03

* Added disabled-by-default `atcf-sanity`, a read-only tropical-cyclone/ATCF
  timeline diagnostic for operational NHC feeds and replay/testing feeds.
* Probes known ASGS ATCF adapters (`get_atcf.pl` and `get_atcf_http.pl`) only
  inside a private temporary directory; it never downloads into or modifies
  the active ASGS run directory.
* Correlates ATCF advisory/model time and forecast extent with ASGS state,
  `COLDSTARTDATE`, `HINDCASTLENGTH`, hotstart `HSTIME`, and current
  `run.properties` / `*.run-control.properties` clocks.
* Detects `forecast_end_time <= advisory_time`, `RunEndTime <= RunStartTime`,
  tiny remaining ADCIRC forecast durations, and the `2*dt` safeguard precursor.
* Detects hotstart model clocks that are ahead of the current ATCF advisory and
  warns when a reused hotstart was produced under a different cold-start epoch.
* Preserves intermediate advisory suffixes such as `002A` when visible in the
  Forecast/Advisory product, while separately reporting adapters that collapse
  the suffix to a numeric advisory.
* Intentionally performs no wall-clock-age failure test; replay and operational
  data are judged by relative model-time invariants.
* Keeps a tiny monitor-owned history keyed by profile configuration/cold-start
  epoch so a distinct next advisory whose model time does not advance is
  reported as CRITICAL without confusing a deliberate replay rebase with age.
* Added an optional `ASGS_MON_RESULT_FILE` JSON sidecar contract so checks can
  attach structured details to status snapshots and future adapter events
  without changing the existing human stdout contract.
* `asgs-mon --check CHECK` now prints the complete diagnostic output for an
  explicit one-shot operator check.
* Added mocked RSS/ATCF regression coverage for intermediate advisories,
  read-only sandboxing, stale/reused hotstarts, collapsed four-second forecasts,
  and forecast-end-at-start failures.

## 0.2.1 - 2026-09-03

* Treats the loaded profile/`ASGS_CONFIG` as the durable monitored identity and
  the `asgs_main.sh` PID as transient runtime state.
* Matches the real `asgs_main.sh -c <canonical ASGS_CONFIG>` argv structure
  instead of basename/substring config matches.
* Revalidates `/proc` candidates and debounces transient Bash fork/subshell
  duplicates before declaring multiple ASGS processes.
* Removes surviving descendant candidates when another matching candidate is
  their ancestor.
* Allows the monitor to start/remain alive while ASGS is absent and
  automatically reacquires a new PID after restart under the same profile.
* Exports process lifecycle state through `ASGS_MON_PROCESS_*`, includes it in
  status/adapter JSON, and clears stale `ASGS_PID` values while waiting.
* `000-asgs_main-pid-check` now reports waiting/ambiguity/restart lifecycle
  state supplied by the supervisor; restart recovery is an immediate NOTICE.
* Added process discovery/debounce and restart/reacquisition regression tests.

## 0.2.0 - 2026-09-01

* Hardened process detection around the loaded `ASGS_CONFIG`; ambiguous matches
  now require `--pid` instead of selecting the lowest PID.
* Added one-monitor-per-profile locking.
* Replaced shell-string check execution and sendmail invocation with list-form
  process execution.
* Enforced per-check timeouts and normalized bad/empty check results to UNKNOWN.
* Changed notification throttling to transition/escalation/hush semantics so
  persistent CRITICAL conditions do not email every monitor pass.
* Refreshes ASGS state each pass and exports normalized `ASGS_MON_*` context.
* Retained the legacy eight positional plugin arguments.
* Added `--once`, `--check`, `--list`, `--enable`, `--disable`, `--validate`,
  and `--status`.
* Running monitors now rescan `active/` each pass, so check enable/disable
  changes take effect without restart.
* Expanded the Bash helper into a robust check API with safe color setup,
  alert helpers, requirements, scheduling, file-age helpers, and compatibility
  accessors.
* Removed state-file `source`/evaluation from Bash helpers/checks.
* Fixed known check issues: JSON warnings on STDOUT, queue state output,
  STATEFILE error status, RUNDIR unit reporting, failed-dir diagnostics,
  SYSLOG rotation/truncation, quoting/word splitting, and TTY handling.
* Added atomic heartbeat/status JSON for external supervision and
  `asgs-mon --status`.
* Added a disabled-by-default adapter seam and JSONL example for future central
  dashboard integration.
* Added check templates, tests, CI, and an optional ASGS `fetch` integration
  patch.
* Uses `Util::H2O::More` conservatively for options/config/runtime objects and
  `Dispatch::Fu` for top-level command dispatch.
